# meridian.spline — a freeform b-spline meridian for spline_cap.cam.
# The (r, z) control polygon of a cubic surface-of-revolution cap, in mm,
# stored apex-first (apex on the axis at the top, base rim at the bottom).
# Both coordinate sequences are monotone — r non-decreasing, z non-increasing —
# so the revolved surface is a machinable cap with no undercut. It is a genuine
# freeform curve, not a circle/parabola/ogive arc, so recognition cannot name
# it as a primitive: exactly the face the analytic NURBS reader exists for.
degree 3
knots 0 0 0 0 0.3333333333333333 0.6666666666666666 1 1 1 1
pole 0 20
pole 3 19
pole 7 16
pole 10 11
pole 12 5
pole 13 0
